IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gaa-incapacity`

-- Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the
-- situation as parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment, following the Graffiti Vandalism
-- Act encoding's design (D2, D4, D8). Every exported question takes `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"); a
-- question about another role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input, so the site's question
-- form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. Four people the Act gives rights to or puts duties on:
--   - the adult planning for incapacity, and the person for whom a guardian or administrator may be appointed (the
--     baseline's seat): the three instruments (Parts 9, 9A, 9B), Tribunal orders (ss 43, 64, 106, 108), and who decides
--     (ss 110ZD, 110ZJ, 119);
--   - the attorney under an enduring power of attorney, or the person asked to be one: eligibility (s 104C), when the
--     power is in force (ss 104B, 105, 106) and the attorney's duties (s 107);
--   - the enduring guardian, or the person asked to be one: eligibility (s 110D), when and for what the guardian may act
--     (ss 110F, 110G, 45), and joint guardians (ss 110H, 53, 54);
--   - the spouse or partner, relative, carer or friend of a patient: who is the person responsible (s 110ZD) and when
--     that person decides treatment (s 110ZJ(5)).
-- The State Administrative Tribunal, the Public Advocate, the Public Trustee and health professionals acting as such are
-- not seats here: what the Tribunal may do appears as what it means for the person asking. A guardian or administrator
-- appointed by the Tribunal is not a seat in this layer (their duties, Parts 4 to 6, are outside the baseline's scope).
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8). A question that arises only in a situation takes that situation's fact straight after
-- `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it is FALSE, without reading anything else. The questions of one
-- situation share one input with the same name, type and @desc. There are seven, all BOOLEAN:
--   - `I have made an enduring power of attorney` (the person): the seven questions about my power -- created validly,
--     in force, a s 106 declaration, the substitute, the attorney's fine, renunciation, an administrator (s 108);
--   - `I have made an enduring power of guardianship` (the person): the five about my power -- valid, my guardian
--     acting now and for this decision, joint guardians agreeing, survivors acting;
--   - `I have made an advance health directive` (the person): the five about my directive -- the form, validity, a
--     treatment decision valid, revoked, operating;
--   - `I have been appointed someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` (the attorney): the seven of
--     ss 104B, 105-107 (all but eligibility);
--   - `I have been appointed someone's enduring guardian` (the enduring guardian): when and for what I may act;
--   - `I am one of two or more joint enduring guardians` (the enduring guardian): the two of ss 110H, 53, 54;
--   - `treatment is proposed for them and they cannot make reasonable judgments about it` (the partner, relative, carer
--     or friend): whether I decide (s 110ZJ(1), (5)).
-- The other questions arise in every situation of their role and take none.
--
-- The rules are in gaa-incapacity.l4. This module calls them and restates none: for the person, each answer is the
-- baseline export's own answer, wrapped in this layer's answer types; for the other roles the baseline's functions are
-- called with that role's facts, and the few duties the baseline has no function for (s 107(1)(a), (b), (d)) are helpers
-- here. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me`
    `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney`
    `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's enduring guardian`
    `I am the partner, relative, carer or friend of someone who may need treatment decided for them`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Age` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `aged` HAS `the completed years` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Whether a guardian may be appointed` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `yes: the Tribunal may appoint a guardian for you now`
    `yes, from your 18th birthday: the Tribunal may appoint a guardian for you, to take effect then`
    `no: the Tribunal may not appoint a guardian for you`

DECLARE `What an administrator means for my power` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the Tribunal must revoke or vary your power to remove the inconsistency`
    `the Tribunal may revoke or vary your power, and your attorney answers to your administrator`

DECLARE `How it may be revoked` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `you may revoke it yourself`
    `your administrator may revoke it, or the Tribunal`
    `only the Tribunal may revoke it`
    `the Act gives the Tribunal power to revoke it and is silent on revocation by you`
    `a treatment decision in it is revoked if you change your mind`

DECLARE `Nearest relative` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the spouse or de facto partner`
    `a child`
    `a parent`
    `a sibling`
    `no relative on the list in s 110ZD(4)`

DECLARE `Person responsible` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the spouse or de facto partner who lives with you`
    `your nearest relative who is close to you`
    `your unpaid primary carer`
    `another adult who is close to you`
    `no person responsible`

DECLARE `Who decides` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `you decide yourself`
    `the treatment decision in your directive`
    `your enduring guardian`
    `your guardian appointed by the Tribunal`
    `your person responsible`
    `no-one under the section`

-- How the partner, relative, carer or friend stands to the patient: the four kinds of person in s 110ZD(3), in its order.
DECLARE `How I stand to the patient` IS ONE OF
    `their spouse or de facto partner, aged 18 or more, living with them`
    `their nearest relative (s 110ZD(4)), with a close personal relationship with them`
    `their unpaid primary carer, aged 18 or more`
    `another adult with a close personal relationship with them`
    `none of these`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

GIVEN `the outcome` IS A GuardianshipOutcome
GIVETH A `Whether a guardian may be appointed`
`the guardianship answer for` `the outcome` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the outcome`
    WHEN `the Tribunal may appoint a guardian for me now` THEN `yes: the Tribunal may appoint a guardian for you now`
    WHEN `the Tribunal may appoint a guardian for me from my 18th birthday` THEN `yes, from your 18th birthday: the Tribunal may appoint a guardian for you, to take effect then`
    WHEN `the Tribunal may not appoint a guardian for me` THEN `no: the Tribunal may not appoint a guardian for you`

GIVEN `the effect` IS AN AdministrationEffect
GIVETH A `What an administrator means for my power`
`the administration answer for` `the effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the effect`
    WHEN `the Tribunal must revoke or vary my power to remove the inconsistency` THEN `the Tribunal must revoke or vary your power to remove the inconsistency`
    WHEN `the Tribunal may revoke or vary my power, and my attorney answers to my administrator` THEN `the Tribunal may revoke or vary your power, and your attorney answers to your administrator`

GIVEN `the revocation` IS A Revocation
GIVETH A `How it may be revoked`
`the revocation answer for` `the revocation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the revocation`
    WHEN `I may revoke it myself` THEN `you may revoke it yourself`
    WHEN `my administrator may revoke it, or the Tribunal` THEN `your administrator may revoke it, or the Tribunal`
    WHEN `only the Tribunal may revoke it` THEN `only the Tribunal may revoke it`
    WHEN `the Act gives the Tribunal power to revoke it and is silent on revocation by me` THEN `the Act gives the Tribunal power to revoke it and is silent on revocation by you`
    WHEN `a treatment decision is revoked if I change my mind` THEN `a treatment decision in it is revoked if you change your mind`

GIVEN `the relative` IS A Relative
GIVETH A `Nearest relative`
`the nearest relative answer for` `the relative` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the relative`
    WHEN `my spouse or de facto partner` THEN `the spouse or de facto partner`
    WHEN `my child` THEN `a child`
    WHEN `my parent` THEN `a parent`
    WHEN `my sibling` THEN `a sibling`
    WHEN `no relative on the list` THEN `no relative on the list in s 110ZD(4)`

GIVEN `the person` IS A ResponsiblePerson
GIVETH A `Person responsible`
`the person responsible answer for` `the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `my spouse or de facto partner who lives with me` THEN `the spouse or de facto partner who lives with you`
    WHEN `my nearest relative who is close to me` THEN `your nearest relative who is close to you`
    WHEN `my unpaid primary carer` THEN `your unpaid primary carer`
    WHEN `another adult who is close to me` THEN `another adult who is close to you`
    WHEN `no person responsible` THEN `no person responsible`

GIVEN `the decider` IS A Decider
GIVETH A `Who decides`
`the decider answer for` `the decider` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decider`
    WHEN `I decide myself` THEN `you decide yourself`
    WHEN `the treatment decision in my directive` THEN `the treatment decision in your directive`
    WHEN `my enduring guardian` THEN `your enduring guardian`
    WHEN `my guardian` THEN `your guardian appointed by the Tribunal`
    WHEN `my person responsible` THEN `your person responsible`
    WHEN `no-one under the section` THEN `no-one under the section`

-- s 107(1): the donee "(a) shall exercise his powers as attorney with reasonable diligence to protect the interests of the
-- donor and, if he fails to do so, he is liable to the donor for any loss occasioned by the failure; (b) shall keep and
-- preserve accurate records and accounts of all dealings and transactions made under the power; ... (d) shall, if the
-- donee becomes bankrupt, report that bankruptcy to the State Administrative Tribunal."
GIVEN `I exercised my powers with reasonable diligence to protect the donor's interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the donor suffered loss because of that failure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 107(1)(a) -- the donee is liable to the donor for the loss` IF
        (NOT `I exercised my powers with reasonable diligence to protect the donor's interests`)
    AND `the donor suffered loss because of that failure`

-- s 110ZD(2), (3): the person responsible is the first, in the order of (3), who is of full legal capacity, reasonably
-- available and willing. Asked from the seat of one of the four: the baseline's `Who is my person responsible` is run
-- with every kind above mine set to whether someone of that kind qualifies, mine set TRUE, and the kinds below FALSE; I am
-- the person responsible if it names my kind. Whether I am of full legal capacity, available and willing is read first.
GIVEN `how I stand to them` IS A `How I stand to the patient`
      `I am of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing to decide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone higher on the list is of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 110ZD -- I am the person responsible` IF
    CONSIDER `how I stand to them`
    WHEN `their spouse or de facto partner, aged 18 or more, living with them` THEN
        `I am of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing to decide`
        AND ((`Who is my person responsible` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `my spouse or de facto partner who lives with me`)
    WHEN `their nearest relative (s 110ZD(4)), with a close personal relationship with them` THEN
        `I am of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing to decide`
        AND ((`Who is my person responsible` `someone higher on the list is of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `my nearest relative who is close to me`)
    WHEN `their unpaid primary carer, aged 18 or more` THEN
        `I am of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing to decide`
        AND ((`Who is my person responsible` `someone higher on the list is of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing` `someone higher on the list is of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `my unpaid primary carer`)
    WHEN `another adult with a close personal relationship with them` THEN
        `I am of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing to decide`
        AND ((`Who is my person responsible` `someone higher on the list is of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing` `someone higher on the list is of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing` `someone higher on the list is of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing` TRUE) EQUALS `another adult who is close to me`)
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE

§§ `For the person planning for incapacity, or for whom a guardian or administrator may be appointed`

§§§ `ss 4, 43, 64 -- capacity, and the Tribunal's orders`

@export How old am I, in completed years, on a given day?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `birth year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year you were born
      `birth month` IS A NUMBER @desc The month you were born (1-12)
      `birth day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month you were born
      `on year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day in question
      `on month` IS A NUMBER @desc The month of the day in question
      `on day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day in question
GIVETH AN `Age`
`How old am I on this day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN `aged` (`How old am I` `birth year` `birth month` `birth day` `on year` `on month` `on day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I presumed capable of managing my own affairs and making my own decisions (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 4(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Tribunal has been satisfied of the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contrary has been proved to the satisfaction of the State Administrative Tribunal
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I presumed capable of managing my own affairs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN `yes if` (`Am I presumed capable` `the Tribunal has been satisfied of the contrary`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the State Administrative Tribunal appoint a guardian for me (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 4(4), 43)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years
      `the Tribunal is satisfied I am incapable of looking after my own health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 43(1)(b)(i), as the Tribunal finds it (for a 17-year-old: will be, at 18)
      `the Tribunal is satisfied I am unable to make reasonable judgments about my person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 43(1)(b)(ii), as the Tribunal finds it (for a 17-year-old: will be, at 18)
      `the Tribunal is satisfied I need oversight, care or control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 43(1)(b)(iii): for your own health and safety or to protect others
      `the Tribunal is satisfied I am in need of a guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 43(1)(c)
      `the Tribunal thinks my needs could be met by less restrictive means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 4(4): for example, by an enduring guardian or an enduring power of attorney you have already made
GIVETH A `Whether a guardian may be appointed`
`Can the Tribunal appoint a guardian for me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN `the guardianship answer for` (`Can a guardian be appointed for me` `my age` `the Tribunal is satisfied I am incapable of looking after my own health and safety` `the Tribunal is satisfied I am unable to make reasonable judgments about my person` `the Tribunal is satisfied I need oversight, care or control` `the Tribunal is satisfied I am in need of a guardian` `the Tribunal thinks my needs could be met by less restrictive means`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the State Administrative Tribunal appoint an administrator of my estate (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 4(4), 64)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Tribunal is satisfied that because of a mental disability I cannot make reasonable judgments about my estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc ss 64(1)(a), 106(2)(b): all or any part of your estate; a mental disability includes an intellectual disability, a psychiatric condition, an acquired brain injury and dementia
      `the Tribunal is satisfied I am in need of an administrator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 64(1)(b)
      `the Tribunal thinks my needs could be met by less restrictive means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 4(4): for example, by an enduring guardian or an enduring power of attorney you have already made
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Tribunal appoint an administrator of my estate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN `yes if` (`Can an administrator be appointed for me` `the Tribunal is satisfied that because of a mental disability I cannot make reasonable judgments about my estate` `the Tribunal is satisfied I am in need of an administrator` `the Tribunal thinks my needs could be met by less restrictive means`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 104(1a), 104C, 110B, 110D, 110P -- making an instrument, and whom I may appoint`

@export May I make an enduring power of attorney, an enduring power of guardianship or an advance health directive (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 104(1a), 110B, 110P)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the instrument` IS AN Instrument @desc Which of the three instruments: an enduring power of attorney, an enduring power of guardianship or an advance health directive
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years
      `I have full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have full legal capacity now (not defined by the Act)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I make this instrument` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN `yes if` (`May I make the instrument` `the instrument` `my age` `I have full legal capacity`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I appoint this person as my attorney or enduring guardian (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 104C, 110D)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the instrument` IS AN Instrument @desc Which of the three instruments: an enduring power of attorney, an enduring power of guardianship or an advance health directive
      `their age` IS A NUMBER @desc The other person's age in completed years
      `they have full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person has full legal capacity
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I appoint this person under my instrument` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN `yes if` (`May I appoint this person` `the instrument` `their age` `they have full legal capacity`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How can my enduring power of attorney, enduring power of guardianship or advance health directive be revoked (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 108, 109, 110N, 110S(6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the instrument` IS AN Instrument @desc Which of the three instruments: an enduring power of attorney, an enduring power of guardianship or an advance health directive
      `I have full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have full legal capacity now (not defined by the Act)
      `an administrator of my estate has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has appointed an administrator for your estate
GIVETH A `How it may be revoked`
`How can this instrument of mine be revoked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN `the revocation answer for` (`How can my instrument be revoked` `the instrument` `I have full legal capacity` `an administrator of my estate has been appointed`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Part 9 -- my enduring power of attorney`

-- Situation: I have made an enduring power of attorney. Each question here is about that power.

@export Is my enduring power of attorney validly created (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 104, Schedule 3)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an enduring power of attorney
      `my power of attorney` IS AN AttorneyInstrument @desc How the enduring power of attorney was made and witnessed
      `my age when I made it` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years when you made the instrument
      `I had full legal capacity when I made it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had full legal capacity when you made the instrument
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my enduring power of attorney valid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an enduring power of attorney`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is my enduring power of attorney validly created` `my power of attorney` `my age when I made it` `I had full legal capacity when I made it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my enduring power of attorney in force now (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 104(1)(b), 105, 106)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an enduring power of attorney
      `the kind` IS AN AttorneyKind @desc Which declaration the enduring power of attorney makes: that it continues despite the donor's later incapacity, or that it is in force only while a s 106 declaration is in force
      `a section 106 declaration is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has declared under s 106 that the donor (you, if the power is yours) does not have legal capacity, and that declaration is in force
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my enduring power of attorney in force now` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an enduring power of attorney`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is my enduring power of attorney in force` `the kind` `a section 106 declaration is in force`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the Tribunal declare under s 106 that I do not have legal capacity, so that my power of attorney springs into force (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 106)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an enduring power of attorney
      `the kind` IS AN AttorneyKind @desc Which declaration the enduring power of attorney makes: that it continues despite the donor's later incapacity, or that it is in force only while a s 106 declaration is in force
      `the Tribunal is satisfied that because of a mental disability I cannot make reasonable judgments about my estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc ss 64(1)(a), 106(2)(b): all or any part of your estate; a mental disability includes an intellectual disability, a psychiatric condition, an acquired brain injury and dementia
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Tribunal declare that I lack legal capacity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an enduring power of attorney`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can the Tribunal declare I lack legal capacity` `the kind` `the Tribunal is satisfied that because of a mental disability I cannot make reasonable judgments about my estate`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Has my substitute attorney become my attorney (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 104B(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an enduring power of attorney
      `the events or circumstances the power specifies for the substitute have occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the events or circumstances specified in paragraph 1a of the enduring power of attorney, for the substitute attorney to act, have happened
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Has my substitute attorney become my attorney yet` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an enduring power of attorney`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Has my substitute attorney become my attorney` `the events or circumstances the power specifies for the substitute have occurred`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most my attorney can be fined for not keeping records and accounts (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 107(1)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an enduring power of attorney
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most my attorney can be fined for not keeping records and accounts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an enduring power of attorney`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount `What is the most my attorney can be fined for not keeping records`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my attorney give up (renounce) my enduring power of attorney (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 107(1)(c), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an enduring power of attorney
      `I am legally incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, at the time, under a legal incapacity
      `the Tribunal has made an order on my attorney's application under s 109(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has revoked or varied the power, or appointed a substitute, on your attorney's own application
      `the power is a recognised interstate or foreign power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the power was made outside Western Australia and recognised by the Tribunal under s 104A(2)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my attorney renounce my enduring power of attorney` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an enduring power of attorney`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my attorney renounce` `I am legally incapable` `the Tribunal has made an order on my attorney's application under s 109(2)` `the power is a recognised interstate or foreign power`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What happens to my enduring power of attorney if the Tribunal appoints an administrator for my estate (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 108)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an enduring power of attorney
      `the power would be inconsistent with the administrator's functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 108(1a): whether the power's continued operation would be inconsistent with what the administrator is to do
GIVETH A `What an administrator means for my power`
`What happens to my power of attorney if an administrator is appointed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an enduring power of attorney`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the administration answer for` (`What happens to my power if an administrator is appointed` `the power would be inconsistent with the administrator's functions`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Part 9A -- my enduring power of guardianship`

-- Situation: I have made an enduring power of guardianship. Each question here is about that power. "Could a plenary
-- guardian make this decision" (s 45) is not about my power, and takes none.

@export Is my enduring power of guardianship valid (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 110E, Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an enduring power of guardianship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an enduring power of guardianship appointing an enduring guardian
      `my power of guardianship` IS A GuardianshipInstrument @desc How the enduring power of guardianship was made, signed, accepted and witnessed
      `my age when I made it` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years when you made the instrument
      `I had full legal capacity when I made it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had full legal capacity when you made the instrument
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my enduring power of guardianship valid under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an enduring power of guardianship`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is my enduring power of guardianship valid` `my power of guardianship` `my age when I made it` `I had full legal capacity when I made it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my enduring guardian act for me now (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 110F, 110G(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an enduring power of guardianship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an enduring power of guardianship appointing an enduring guardian
      `I am unable to make reasonable judgments about matters relating to my person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cannot, at the time, make reasonable judgments about your own person
      `the circumstances the power limits it to exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If section 5 of the enduring power of guardianship limits when the guardian may act, whether those circumstances exist; answer yes if it sets no limit
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my enduring guardian act for me at this time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an enduring power of guardianship`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my enduring guardian act for me now` `I am unable to make reasonable judgments about matters relating to my person` `the circumstances the power limits it to exist`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Could a plenary guardian make this decision about me (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 45)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the decision` IS A PersonalDecision @desc The decision to be made, worded as the person it is about (the appointor) would put it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Could a plenary guardian make this decision about me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN `yes if` (`Could a plenary guardian make this decision` `the decision`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my enduring guardian make this decision for me (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 110F, 110G, 45)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an enduring power of guardianship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an enduring power of guardianship appointing an enduring guardian
      `the decision` IS A PersonalDecision @desc The decision to be made, worded as the person it is about (the appointor) would put it
      `I am unable to make reasonable judgments about matters relating to my person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cannot, at the time, make reasonable judgments about your own person
      `the power limits the functions or circumstances so as to exclude it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether sections 4B or 5 of the enduring power of guardianship leave this decision out
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my enduring guardian make this decision about me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an enduring power of guardianship`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my enduring guardian make this decision` `the decision` `I am unable to make reasonable judgments about matters relating to my person` `the power limits the functions or circumstances so as to exclude it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my joint enduring guardians all agree before acting (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 110H(b), 53(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an enduring power of guardianship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an enduring power of guardianship appointing an enduring guardian
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my joint enduring guardians all agree` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an enduring power of guardianship`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` `Must my joint enduring guardians agree`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If one of my joint enduring guardians dies, may the survivors act (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 110H(c), 54)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an enduring power of guardianship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an enduring power of guardianship appointing an enduring guardian
      `the power says the survivors are not to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the enduring power of guardianship keeps section 3B of the form (surviving joint enduring guardians not to act)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my surviving joint enduring guardians act after a death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an enduring power of guardianship`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my surviving joint enduring guardians act` `the power says the survivors are not to act`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Part 9B -- my advance health directive`

-- Situation: I have made an advance health directive. Each question here is about that directive.

@export Was the form I used the prescribed advance health directive form on the day I made it (Guardianship and Administration Regulations 2005 (WA) regs 7, 9)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an advance health directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an advance health directive
      `the form` IS A DirectiveForm @desc Which form you used
      `year made` IS A NUMBER @desc The year you made the directive
      `month made` IS A NUMBER @desc The month you made the directive
      `day made` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month you made the directive
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was the form of my directive the prescribed form` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an advance health directive`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Was my directive form prescribed` `the form` `year made` `month made` `day made`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my advance health directive valid (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 110P, 110Q)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an advance health directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an advance health directive
      `my directive` IS A Directive @desc How the directive was made, signed and witnessed, and how many treatment decisions it contains
      `my age when I made it` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years when you made the instrument
      `I had full legal capacity when I made it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had full legal capacity when you made the instrument
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my advance health directive valid under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an advance health directive`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is my advance health directive valid` `my directive` `my age when I made it` `I had full legal capacity when I made it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is this treatment decision in my directive valid (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 110R)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an advance health directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an advance health directive
      `I made it voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made the decision of your own free will
      `I made it because of inducement or coercion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were induced or pressured into it
      `I understood its nature and consequences when I made it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you made the directive, you understood what the decision was and what would follow from it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is this treatment decision of mine valid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an advance health directive`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is my treatment decision valid` `I made it voluntarily` `I made it because of inducement or coercion` `I understood its nature and consequences when I made it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is a treatment decision in my directive revoked (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 110S(6), 110T)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an advance health directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an advance health directive
      `I have changed my mind about it since making the directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have changed your mind about the decision
      `the only sign of that is a later enduring power of guardianship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only evidence is that you later appointed an enduring guardian
      `I ticked the revocation statement in a later directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a later Schedule 2 directive of yours revokes all prior directives
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is this treatment decision of mine revoked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an advance health directive`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is my treatment decision revoked` `I have changed my mind about it since making the directive` `the only sign of that is a later enduring power of guardianship` `I ticked the revocation statement in a later directive`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does a treatment decision in my directive operate now (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 110S)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made an advance health directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or signed, an advance health directive
      `I am unable to make reasonable judgments about the treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cannot, at the time, make reasonable judgments about this treatment
      `the circumstances are ones my directive specifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision was made for circumstances like these
      `the circumstances are ones I would not reasonably have anticipated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110S(3)(a)
      `they would have made a reasonable person in my position change their mind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110S(3)(b)
      `the decision is revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision has been revoked (s 110S(6))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this treatment decision of mine operate now` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made an advance health directive`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does my treatment decision operate` `I am unable to make reasonable judgments about the treatment` `the circumstances are ones my directive specifies` `the circumstances are ones I would not reasonably have anticipated` `they would have made a reasonable person in my position change their mind` `the decision is revoked`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 110ZD, 110ZJ, 119 -- who decides for me`

@export Who is my nearest relative for my person responsible (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 110ZD(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have an adult spouse or de facto partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a spouse or de facto partner aged 18 or more
      `I have an adult child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a child aged 18 or more
      `I have an adult parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a parent of yours is alive and aged 18 or more
      `I have an adult sibling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a brother or sister aged 18 or more
GIVETH A `Nearest relative`
`Who is my nearest relative for treatment decisions` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN `the nearest relative answer for` (`Who is my nearest relative` `I have an adult spouse or de facto partner` `I have an adult child` `I have an adult parent` `I have an adult sibling`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my carer count as my unpaid primary carer for my person responsible (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 110ZD(3)(c), (6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `their age` IS A NUMBER @desc The other person's age in completed years
      `they are my primary provider of care and support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your carer is your primary provider of care and support, including emotional support
      `they are paid for it other than by a government carer payment or benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your carer is paid for that care other than by a Commonwealth, State or Territory carer payment or benefit for home care
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my carer count as my unpaid primary carer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN `yes if` (`Is my carer my unpaid primary carer` `their age` `they are my primary provider of care and support` `they are paid for it other than by a government carer payment or benefit`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Who is my person responsible for treatment decisions (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 110ZD)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an adult spouse or partner living with me qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110ZD(3)(a): aged 18 or more, living with you, capable, available and willing
      `my nearest relative is close to me and qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110ZD(3)(b): frequent personal contact and a genuine interest in your welfare; capable, available and willing
      `my unpaid primary carer qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110ZD(3)(c): capable, available and willing
      `another adult close to me qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110ZD(3)(d): capable, available and willing
GIVETH A `Person responsible`
`Who is my person responsible for treatment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN `the person responsible answer for` (`Who is my person responsible` `an adult spouse or partner living with me qualifies` `my nearest relative is close to me and qualifies` `my unpaid primary carer qualifies` `another adult close to me qualifies`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If treatment is proposed, who decides whether I get it (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 110ZJ)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I can make reasonable judgments about the treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can decide for yourself
      `a treatment decision in my directive covers the treatment and operates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc See "Does a treatment decision in my directive operate now"
      `my enduring guardian is authorised, available and willing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110ZJ(3)(b), s 119(2): an enduring guardian you appointed
      `my guardian is authorised, available and willing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110ZJ(4)(b), s 119(3): a guardian appointed by the Tribunal
      `I have a person responsible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc See "Who is my person responsible"
GIVETH A `Who decides`
`Who decides whether I get the proposed treatment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN `the decider answer for` (`Who decides my treatment` `I can make reasonable judgments about the treatment` `a treatment decision in my directive covers the treatment and operates` `my enduring guardian is authorised, available and willing` `my guardian is authorised, available and willing` `I have a person responsible`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export For a personal matter other than treatment or medical research, who decides for me (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 119)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I can make reasonable judgments about the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can decide for yourself
      `my enduring guardian is authorised, available and willing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110ZJ(3)(b), s 119(2): an enduring guardian you appointed
      `my guardian is authorised, available and willing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110ZJ(4)(b), s 119(3): a guardian appointed by the Tribunal
GIVETH A `Who decides`
`Who decides my other personal matters for me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me` THEN `the decider answer for` (`Who decides my other personal matters` `I can make reasonable judgments about the matter` `my enduring guardian is authorised, available and willing` `my guardian is authorised, available and willing`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the attorney under an enduring power of attorney`

§§§ `s 104C -- may I be appointed`

@export May I be appointed as someone's attorney, or substitute attorney, under an enduring power of attorney (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 104C)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years
      `I have full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have full legal capacity now (not defined by the Act)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I be appointed as an attorney under an enduring power of attorney` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` THEN `yes if` (`May I appoint this person` `an enduring power of attorney` `my age` `I have full legal capacity`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 104B, 105, 106, 107 -- acting as attorney, and my duties`

-- Situation: I have been appointed attorney (or substitute attorney) under an enduring power of attorney.

@export May I act under the enduring power of attorney now: is it in force (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 104(1)(b), 105, 106)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been appointed someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an enduring power of attorney names you as its attorney (donee) or substitute attorney, and you have accepted
      `the kind` IS AN AttorneyKind @desc Which declaration the enduring power of attorney makes: that it continues despite the donor's later incapacity, or that it is in force only while a s 106 declaration is in force
      `a section 106 declaration is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has declared under s 106 that the donor (you, if the power is yours) does not have legal capacity, and that declaration is in force
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the enduring power of attorney I hold in force` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been appointed someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is my enduring power of attorney in force` `the kind` `a section 106 declaration is in force`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export I am the substitute attorney: have I become the attorney (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 104B(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been appointed someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an enduring power of attorney names you as its attorney (donee) or substitute attorney, and you have accepted
      `the events or circumstances the power specifies for the substitute have occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the events or circumstances specified in paragraph 1a of the enduring power of attorney, for the substitute attorney to act, have happened
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I become the attorney as substitute` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been appointed someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Has my substitute attorney become my attorney` `the events or circumstances the power specifies for the substitute have occurred`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I keep and preserve accurate records and accounts of all my dealings and transactions under the power (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 107(1)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been appointed someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an enduring power of attorney names you as its attorney (donee) or substitute attorney, and you have accepted
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I keep records and accounts as attorney` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been appointed someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE yes
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for not keeping records and accounts as attorney (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 107(1)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been appointed someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an enduring power of attorney names you as its attorney (donee) or substitute attorney, and you have accepted
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for not keeping records as attorney` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been appointed someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount `What is the most my attorney can be fined for not keeping records`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I give up (renounce) the enduring power of attorney (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 107(1)(c), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been appointed someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an enduring power of attorney names you as its attorney (donee) or substitute attorney, and you have accepted
      `the donor is legally incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who gave you the power is, at the time, under a legal incapacity
      `the Tribunal has made an order on my application under s 109(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has revoked or varied the power, or appointed a substitute, on your own application
      `the power is a recognised interstate or foreign power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the power was made outside Western Australia and recognised by the Tribunal under s 104A(2)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I renounce the enduring power of attorney` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been appointed someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my attorney renounce` `the donor is legally incapable` `the Tribunal has made an order on my application under s 109(2)` `the power is a recognised interstate or foreign power`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I liable to the donor for a loss because I did not act with reasonable diligence to protect their interests (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 107(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been appointed someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an enduring power of attorney names you as its attorney (donee) or substitute attorney, and you have accepted
      `I exercised my powers with reasonable diligence to protect the donor's interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you used your powers as attorney with reasonable diligence to protect the interests of the person who gave you the power
      `the donor suffered loss because of that failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who gave you the power suffered a loss caused by your lack of reasonable diligence
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I liable to the donor for a loss` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been appointed someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`s 107(1)(a) -- the donee is liable to the donor for the loss` `I exercised my powers with reasonable diligence to protect the donor's interests` `the donor suffered loss because of that failure`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I report my bankruptcy to the State Administrative Tribunal (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 107(1)(d))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been appointed someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an enduring power of attorney names you as its attorney (donee) or substitute attorney, and you have accepted
      `I have become bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have become bankrupt
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I report my bankruptcy to the Tribunal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been appointed someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` `I have become bankrupt`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the enduring guardian`

§§§ `s 110D -- may I be appointed`

@export May I be appointed as someone's enduring guardian (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 110D)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years
      `I have full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have full legal capacity now (not defined by the Act)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I be appointed as an enduring guardian` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's enduring guardian` THEN `yes if` (`May I appoint this person` `an enduring power of guardianship` `my age` `I have full legal capacity`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 110F, 110G, 45 -- when and for what I may act`

-- Situation: I have been appointed someone's enduring guardian.

@export May I act as enduring guardian now (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 110F, 110G(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been appointed someone's enduring guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an enduring power of guardianship appoints you as enduring guardian or substitute enduring guardian, and you have signed to accept
      `the appointor is unable to make reasonable judgments about matters relating to their person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who appointed you cannot, at the time, make reasonable judgments about their own person
      `the circumstances the power limits it to exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If section 5 of the enduring power of guardianship limits when the guardian may act, whether those circumstances exist; answer yes if it sets no limit
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I act as enduring guardian now` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's enduring guardian` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been appointed someone's enduring guardian`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my enduring guardian act for me now` `the appointor is unable to make reasonable judgments about matters relating to their person` `the circumstances the power limits it to exist`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I make this decision as enduring guardian (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 110F, 110G, 45)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been appointed someone's enduring guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an enduring power of guardianship appoints you as enduring guardian or substitute enduring guardian, and you have signed to accept
      `the decision` IS A PersonalDecision @desc The decision to be made, worded as the person it is about (the appointor) would put it
      `the appointor is unable to make reasonable judgments about matters relating to their person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who appointed you cannot, at the time, make reasonable judgments about their own person
      `the power limits the functions or circumstances so as to exclude it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether sections 4B or 5 of the enduring power of guardianship leave this decision out
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I make this decision as enduring guardian` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's enduring guardian` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been appointed someone's enduring guardian`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my enduring guardian make this decision` `the decision` `the appointor is unable to make reasonable judgments about matters relating to their person` `the power limits the functions or circumstances so as to exclude it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 110H, 53, 54 -- joint enduring guardians`

-- Situation: I am one of two or more joint enduring guardians (which implies I have been appointed).

@export Must I and my fellow joint enduring guardians all agree before any of us acts (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 110H(b), 53(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am one of two or more joint enduring guardians` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the enduring power of guardianship appoints you jointly with one or more other enduring guardians
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must we joint enduring guardians all agree before acting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's enduring guardian` THEN
        IF NOT `I am one of two or more joint enduring guardians`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` `Must my joint enduring guardians agree`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If one of my fellow joint enduring guardians dies, may we who survive act (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) ss 110H(c), 54)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am one of two or more joint enduring guardians` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the enduring power of guardianship appoints you jointly with one or more other enduring guardians
      `the power says the survivors are not to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the enduring power of guardianship keeps section 3B of the form (surviving joint enduring guardians not to act)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May we surviving joint enduring guardians act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's enduring guardian` THEN
        IF NOT `I am one of two or more joint enduring guardians`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my surviving joint enduring guardians act` `the power says the survivors are not to act`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the partner, relative, carer or friend of a patient`

§§§ `s 110ZD -- the person responsible`

@export Am I the person responsible for the patient, who makes treatment decisions where no-one before me does (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 110ZD(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I stand to them` IS A `How I stand to the patient` @desc Which of the kinds of person in s 110ZD(3) you are to the patient, in its order: their spouse or de facto partner living with them; their nearest relative with a close personal relationship; their unpaid primary carer; another adult with a close personal relationship; or none of these
      `I am of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing to decide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are of full legal capacity, reasonably available, and willing to make a treatment decision for the patient
      `someone higher on the list is of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person of a kind that comes before yours in s 110ZD(3) is of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing to make a treatment decision
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I the person responsible for the patient` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the partner, relative, carer or friend of someone who may need treatment decided for them` THEN `yes if` (`s 110ZD -- I am the person responsible` `how I stand to them` `I am of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing to decide` `someone higher on the list is of full legal capacity, reasonably available and willing`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Who is the patient's nearest relative for their person responsible (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 110ZD(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the patient has an adult spouse or de facto partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the patient has a spouse or de facto partner aged 18 or more
      `the patient has an adult child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the patient has a child aged 18 or more
      `the patient has an adult parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a parent of the patient is alive and aged 18 or more
      `the patient has an adult sibling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the patient has a brother or sister aged 18 or more
GIVETH A `Nearest relative`
`Who is the patient's nearest relative` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the partner, relative, carer or friend of someone who may need treatment decided for them` THEN `the nearest relative answer for` (`Who is my nearest relative` `the patient has an adult spouse or de facto partner` `the patient has an adult child` `the patient has an adult parent` `the patient has an adult sibling`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do I count as the patient's unpaid primary carer (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 110ZD(3)(c), (6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years
      `I am their primary provider of care and support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the patient's primary provider of care and support, including emotional support
      `I am paid for it other than by a government carer payment or benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are paid for that care other than by a Commonwealth, State or Territory carer payment or benefit for home care
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I count as the patient's unpaid primary carer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the partner, relative, carer or friend of someone who may need treatment decided for them` THEN `yes if` (`Is my carer my unpaid primary carer` `my age` `I am their primary provider of care and support` `I am paid for it other than by a government carer payment or benefit`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 110ZJ -- when I decide the patient's treatment`

-- Situation: treatment is proposed for the patient and they cannot make reasonable judgments about it (s 110ZJ(1)).

@export Do I decide whether the patient gets the proposed treatment (Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) s 110ZJ(1)-(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `treatment is proposed for them and they cannot make reasonable judgments about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether treatment is proposed for the patient, and the patient is unable to make reasonable judgments about it
      `a treatment decision in their directive covers the treatment and operates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the patient's advance health directive contains a treatment decision about this treatment that operates now (s 110S)
      `their enduring guardian is authorised, available and willing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an enduring guardian of the patient is authorised to make this treatment decision, reasonably available and willing (s 110ZJ(3))
      `their guardian is authorised, available and willing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a guardian appointed for the patient by the Tribunal is authorised to make this treatment decision, reasonably available and willing (s 110ZJ(4))
      `I am their person responsible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the patient's person responsible (see "Am I the person responsible for the patient")
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I decide whether the patient gets the treatment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the partner, relative, carer or friend of someone who may need treatment decided for them` THEN
        IF NOT `treatment is proposed for them and they cannot make reasonable judgments about it`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` ((`Who decides my treatment` FALSE `a treatment decision in their directive covers the treatment and operates` `their enduring guardian is authorised, available and willing` `their guardian is authorised, available and willing` `I am their person responsible`) EQUALS `my person responsible`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
